==Enemy==
A supersized version of [[Emperor Warumongar]], with surprisingly similar stats all around. The main difference between them and Grand Emperor Warumongar is the latter's newly gained [[Omni Strike]], extending his non-[[Explosion]] reach to 570, now outranging [[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Prime DX]]—his maximum effective range is still 695. Warumongar's attack cycle is even longer now too, at almost 15 seconds, greatly hurting his high damage potential. He is also buffed to ineffable degrees in later encounters, typically becoming the most dangerous threat in any stage he's in.

==Strategy==
Grand Emperor Warumongar's overtly long attack rate is his Achilles' heel: you will want to use nukers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N006 (Special Cat)|Fallen Bear Cat]], as well as [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Ranger]], to accumulate damage on him quickly and efficiently. You can use Giga-Nyan Prime DX in earlier encounters, but by [[Clash with Darkness]], the sheer damage quickly starts becoming too much for the robot to handle for extended periods. Warumongar will usually be the last enemy standing in any stage he's in, so whittle him down and foil his evil stratagem once and for all!

